    "doff": {
      "word": "DOFF",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To put off, as dress; to divest one's self of; hence, figuratively, to put or thrust away; to rid one's self of. And made us doff our easy robes of peace. Shak. At night, or in the rain, He dons a surcoat which he doffs at morn. Emerson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To strip; to divest; to undress. Heaven's King, who doffs himself our flesh to wear. Crashaw.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To put off dress; to take off the hat.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
